# Do not touch line endings. They are load-bearing in this project:
#   - The Windows install's BepInEx.cfg is mixed CRLF/LF, and `deploy.py`'s `set_config_key`
#     preserves them per line so a deploy is not a diff on every run (see its docstring).
#   - `Edi/Gallery/Definitions.csv` is rewritten by the gallery tools, which preserve whatever
#     separators the file already has rather than imposing one.
# Normalising on checkin would make git the thing that decides, silently, for files whose
# endings several tools deliberately leave alone. So every file is treated as binary for the
# purpose of EOL conversion - this says nothing about content, only about conversion.
* -text
